  "story": {
    "intro_title": "A LETTER FROM GRANDPA",
    "intro": "Kiddo,\n\nIf you're reading this, the quarry is yours now. The bank says it's worth nothing. The town says it never made a cent.\n\nThey're wrong. There's good rock in those hills, and better rock under them. I just got too old to dig.\n\nStart small. Use my hammer. Sell what you break. The rest will come.\n\n- Grandpa Walt",
    "discoveries": {
      "first_clear": {
        "title": "GRANDPA'S LOCKBOX",
        "trigger": "first_formation_cleared",
        "text": "Under the last of the rock sits a rusted lockbox. Inside:\n\n- A faded photo of the crew in 1971, standing on this same floor.\n- Mining records: 'Core sample, 3.5 m below the north bench: copper staining, trace gold.'\n- A note: 'Didn't have the machines to go deeper. Maybe you will.'\n\nThere's also an old savings bond. It's still good.",
        "reward": 400
      }
    }
  }
